{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Between me.</b> And in circumcision it is written 'covenant' as well as 'sign,' and likewise regarding Sabbath. And the Gaon [Saadia] said: just as one who is found circumcised with periah — those who find him know that he is from Israel, and likewise when one does no work on the Sabbath, or does not buy and sell on the Sabbath. But in my opinion, the meaning of 'sign' is 'for in six days [YHWH made],' and behold, one who does work on the Sabbath denies the act of Creation." "And the Torah spoke in the language of human beings so that listeners may understand, and said 'and He rested' — for HaShem neither faints nor wearies (Isaiah 40:28). For behold, His creations, which are the noble bodies, which are the hosts of the heavens, revolve forever day and night, and all the more so the noble [beings] that are not bodies, and all the more so the Creator of all, who dwells eternally and sits of old, and His acts are not in motion, rather all is done by His word."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:41.035936225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}